<title>CANADA: Toronto bull run fueling TSE listings boom.</title>
<headline>Toronto bull run fueling TSE listings boom.</headline>
<byline>Lydia Zajc</byline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A bull run in Toronto equities should prompt a slew of new listings from now until year-end, Ralph Shay, the Toronto Stock Exchange's vice-president of company listings and regulation, said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;If the current pace continues, we could have 30 or more,&quot; Shay told Reuters.</p>
<p>Canada's largest stock exchange listed 108 new companies in the first three quarters of 1996, against 56 in the same period a year earlier. However, the showing so far is nowhere that of 1987, when the TSE listed 180 firms in the full year.</p>
